<xml xmlns="https://developers.google.com/blockly/xml"><block type="offer_generic" id="ai00075" x="50" y="50"><comment pinned="true" h="220" w="520">AI draft: Each spend transaction earns points based on its amount. A transaction of $200 or more earns 3x the amount in points, and a transaction under $200 earns 1x. Each member can earn at most 2,000 bonus points from this offer over their lifetime.&#10;&#10;Assumptions:&#10;- 'Spends' is taken as the Spend activity type (SPEND). It could also mean Shopping (PURCHASE).&#10;- The spend amount is read from BIT Amount (h_bit_amount), and the threshold is applied to each transaction on its own, not to cumulative spend.&#10;- '3x points' means points = amount x 3 in total, not 3x on top of base earning. 1x means points = amount x 1.&#10;- '$200 or more' includes exactly $200 (&gt;= 200).&#10;- The 2,000-point lifetime cap applies to all points this offer awards, in both bands.&#10;- No start or end dates were given, so the offer has none. Points go to the DELTA MILES account.</comment><statement name="activities"><block type="activity" id="ai00074"><statement name="ACTIVITY_CRITERIA"><block type="activity_criteria" id="ai00001"><mutation xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1999/xhtml" object="activity" attribute="h_bit_type" operators="in" payoperators="null" iscountertypevector="no" value="SPEND" visible_value="Spend" type="LOOKUP"></mutation><field name="OBJECT">activity</field><field name="attribute">h_bit_type</field><field name="operators">in</field></block></statement><statement name="RULES"><block type="rule" id="ai00020"><field name="IDENTIFIER">Tier 1 capped remainder</field><statement name="CONDITION"><block type="if_generic_adaptive" id="ai00009"><mutation xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1999/xhtml" object="activity" attribute="h_bit_amount" operators="&gt;=" payoperators="null" iscountertypevector="no" type="NUMBER"></mutation><field name="OBJECT">activity</field><field name="attribute">h_bit_amount</field><field name="operators